  "description": "## How we proceed ?\n\n1. To find meaningful segments on the customers, we tested various settings (4,5,6,7 clusters) on the algorithm K-means -- [The full list of available algorithms is here](/projects/DKU_CHURN/analysis/To45m4yi/ml/c/IRL6lq6i/settings/).\n2. The four differents settings result in [3 differents models](/projects/DKU_CHURN/analysis/To45m4yi/ml/c/IRL6lq6i/) that are listed in the tab _Models_.\n\n## Results\n\n1. For each model, we interpreted the resulting segments (clusters) by looking at the charts on the models and on the predicted values.\n2. We then named the clusters of [K-means algorithm model with 6 clusters](/projects/DKU_CHURN/analysis/To45m4yi/ml/c/IRL6lq6i/A-DKU_CHURN-To45m4yi-IRL6lq6i-s3-pp1-m3/report/) by visiting the associated charts on the predicted data.\n3. The model with 6 segments have been deployed in the [flow](/projects/DKU_CHURN/flow/) and is used to map customers each customers in its segment.\n\n## Visit the segmentation insights\n\nTry to interpret yourself these segments, by visiting :\n\n1. the [heatmap](/projects/DKU_CHURN/analysis/To45m4yi/ml/c/IRL6lq6i/A-DKU_CHURN-To45m4yi-IRL6lq6i-s3-pp1-m3/report/#heatmap)\n2. and [custom charts](/projects/DKU_CHURN/analysis/To45m4yi/ml/c/IRL6lq6i/A-DKU_CHURN-To45m4yi-IRL6lq6i-s3-pp1-m3/charts/)\n\n\nNote : In this analysis, we neither do cleansing nor create new features but if needed, this could have been done in the _Script_ tab.",
